{"title":"XIII CONCLUSION","paras":[
"FA-MAS reframes reliable agent execution as constrained recovery of a stateful service composition. The design combines contracts, failure-belief estimation, a proposed recomposition frontier and compensation-aware state recovery. Only reduced gates, finite-action selection and local service state are currently executable. The original simulator favors FA-MAS on recorded safety under unequal authored diagnosis parameters. The initial matched study is negative. After disclosed defect corrections, the exploratory simulator favors gated selection over two controls but shows no resolved benefit from compensation; orphan-state failures persist. No live-model advantage has been measured.",
"That negative boundary is the principal empirical lesson: service safety and task completion are distinct objectives. A runtime can finish more tasks by taking actions that violate authorization or leave inconsistent state. FA-MAS makes that tradeoff explicit and auditable.",
"The paper's defensible contribution is a reference specification and transparent mechanism evaluation; the matched and corrected sensitivity studies prevent an unconditional claim of safety superiority. It is a services-computing control architecture, formal objective, executable recovery protocol, and reproducible fault-injection methodology. Completion of the prespecified live-model protocol would strengthen external validity without changing the contract and state semantics evaluated here.",
"ACKNOWLEDGMENT",
"OpenAI ChatGPT and Codex assisted with drafting and revising Sections I–XIII, generating evaluation source code and figures, and preparing analysis scripts. The author is responsible for checking the scientific content, citations, code, and results before submission. Funding and author contribution disclosures require the author's confirmation.",
"APPENDIX A CONTRACT MANIFEST EXCERPT",
"service: refund; input: case_id, account_id, amount, currency, idempotency_key; preconditions: verified account and eligible policy; postconditions: one ledger entry linked to case; state: idempotent_write; reconcile: GET /refunds/by-key/{key}; compensate: POST /refunds/{id}/reverse; scopes: refund:write; approval: amount above configured threshold; alternatives: refund_backup; timeout and cost profiles: deployment specific.",
"APPENDIX B CLAIM CHECK",
"Supported with limitations: the reference simulator implements the reduced contract fields and recovery actions described in Section VII; it generated the reported observations; historical paired comparisons reproduce the recorded effects under unequal authored parameters and a weaker terminal judge. The initial matched exploratory study is negative; the corrected study remains conditional and does not establish production or live-model superiority. The artifact also implements the Tier 2 adapters, task split, protocol lock, transactional judge, trace hashing, and analysis gate. Not supported: full implementation of every architectural field, production readiness, exactly-once execution for arbitrary providers, universal model superiority, or live-LLM generality before Tier 2 execution." ]},
