                       "The held-out instances change workflow length, SKU and capacity; they are authored variants of known fault families, not unseen production tasks. Four development tasks are disjoint. Fifty-two unit tests pass and eight scripted development trajectories complete, all marked non-live. The lock covers code, task bank, model endpoints and rates, and runtime versions. Provider failures remain in the data; incomplete matrices cannot enter the live comparison. Local hashing is not independent preregistration.",
